  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n   We propose a novel method based on **multi-scale harmonic optimization** combined with **stochastic projection** of constraints. The core idea is to represent the step function \\(h(x)\\) using a Chebyshev orthogonal polynomial basis truncated at degree \\(N\\), ensuring exact satisfaction of integral constraints while promoting smooth decay in autocorrelation entropy. This approach differs fundamentally from gradient-based optimization as it:\n\n   - Uses mathematical spectra to escape local optima\n   - Formulates energy minimization via quadratic interpolation  \n   - Employs dimension reduction through adaptive frequency weighting  \n   - Handles periodic boundary conditions through inclusion of higher modes  \n\n   The recorded bound suggests the optimal solution may lie in a linearly-constrained subspace of Fourier basis elements. Our experiments indicate this spectral approach can flatten the loss landscape, enabling discovery of sparser energy landscapes compared to standard methods.\n\n   Key limitations: Computation requires condition number checks for ill-conditioned projections; entropy decay tracking may introduce numerical drift; frequency sampling assumes uniform energy distribution a-priori.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n   We represent \\(h(x)\\) on \\([0,2]\\) using the first \\(N\\) Chebyshev polynomials \\(T_0(x),\\ldots,T_{N-1}(x)\\):\n   \\[\n   h(x) = \\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} a_k T_k(x) \\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\int_0^2 h(x)dx=1\n   \\]\n   Constraints are enforced via Lagrange multipliers directly. The squared energy is minimized:\n   \\[\n   E = \\max_k \\left[ \\int_0^2 h(x)h(x+k)dx \\right]^{-1}\n   \\]\n   where relevant variables must pass null-space checks (computed discretely via Legendre-Gauss quadrature). Sampling points are taken from \\(X \\sim \\mathcal{U}[0,2]\\) to ensure uniform coverage.\n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n   Steps from initialization to termination:\n   - `def setup_basis(n)`: Creates orthogonal Chebyshev basis \\(\\{T_k(x)\\}_{k=0}^{N}\\) with \\(N\u2248\\sqrt{n}\\)\n   - `def constrain_matrix(basis)`: Builds constraint matrix via quadrature; \\(\\mathbf{A} = \\int_0^2 basis \\cdot dx\\)\n   - `def project_onto_stable_subspace(M)`: Eigenvalue decomposition to isolate stable modes\n   - `def spectral_gram_schmidt(basis)`: Orthonormalizes using energy-normalization\n   - `def run_spectral_phase(samples, max_iters=5000)`:\n        1. Initialize coefficients from parent solution\n        2. Apply Jacobi preconditioner to modal coupling matrix\n        3. Perform gradient descent with 3rd-order momentum amortization\n        4. Inject noise proportional to \\(\\exp(-iter/\\tau)\\) for early escape\n\n   Coefficients are clipped to [0,1] projection except constants. Transformation from parent solution is achieved by:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{a}_{new} = \\mathbf{A}^{\\dagger}\\mathbf{a}_{parent} + \\arg\\min_{\\mathbf{b}} \\|proj_{orth}\\mathbf{b} - \\xi\\|_2^2\n   \\]\n   where \\(\\xi\\) contains regularization terms for filtering.\n\n4. Search choices and variations  \n   - Primary frequency components: weights decay as \\(w_k = \\exp(-k^2/c^2)\\) with \\(c=4\\)\n   - Global restarts triggered when: \\|\u2207E\\|/E > 10^{-3} or relative improvement < 1e-4\n   - Frequency annealing:\n        \\[\\alpha_k = \\alpha_{\\min} + (\\alpha_{\\max} - \\alpha_{\\min}) \\exp(-k^2/T)\\]\n   - Orthogonality threshold: \\( \\|T_k \\cdot T_j\\| < 1e-10 \\)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n   - Dominant cost: O(N\u00b3) operations per spectral component; recommended N=40 for simulation\n   - Wall-clock: 900 seconds minimum, execute phase N=100 bounded by hessian-vector products\n   - Out-of-memory: requires storing 20-D latent space in float32; parent solution validation via L1-penalized recovery\n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n   - Feasibility: \\(\\int h dx / dx - 1 < 1e-12\\) and \\([0,1]^n\\) projections\n   - Objective check: recompute exact integral using Simpson's rule not basis approximation\n   - Energy monitoring: stores minimum, maximum and mean deviations in stats array\n   - Return format: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points) with h_values clipped to [0,1]\n   - Fallback: If computation fails, return parent solution projected onto stable basis\n\n   Note: This implementation requires careful null-space management during projection.",
